1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,940
Once upon a time, there was a man who died.

2
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:10,180
The man had the power to make stories come true,

3
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,160
so his hands were cut off by the people,

4
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:16,940
who were afraid of tragedies becoming reality.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,080
When the man died, the people heaved a great sigh of relief.

6
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:26,380
As it turned out, however, when his hands were cut off,

7
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:30,060
the man had been writing a story in his own blood.

8
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:35,600
That was a story he could continue spinning even after he died.

9
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,580
A story of the man himself.

10
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:28,395
Oh!

11
00:02:28,395 --> 00:02:30,395
What?

12
00:02:30,395 --> 00:02:32,395
This can't be!

13
00:02:32,395 --> 00:02:36,395
To think the words of true love, Tutu was supposed to say.

14
00:02:36,395 --> 00:02:39,395
Princess Crayhe ended up saying it stiff,

15
00:02:39,395 --> 00:02:42,395
even though she was raised on Raven's blood

16
00:02:42,395 --> 00:02:46,395
and shouldn't even know how to love.

17
00:02:46,395 --> 00:02:49,395
Regardless, you still will be unable to escape tragedy,

18
00:02:49,395 --> 00:02:52,395
my dear little duck.

19
00:02:55,395 --> 00:03:14,395
Princess Crayhe

20
00:03:14,395 --> 00:03:16,395
Are you glad to have it, Prince?

21
00:03:16,395 --> 00:03:18,395
I don't know.

22
00:03:18,395 --> 00:03:21,395
Seiya, I have another question.

23
00:03:21,395 --> 00:03:23,395
Do you think you'll love me?

24
00:03:23,395 --> 00:03:26,395
I don't know.

25
00:03:26,395 --> 00:03:28,395
Well, just tell me you love me.

26
00:03:28,395 --> 00:03:30,395
I love you.

27
00:03:30,395 --> 00:03:33,395
I want to hear you say that you love me.

28
00:03:33,395 --> 00:03:36,395
Trust me, Muto, you do love me.

29
00:03:36,395 --> 00:03:38,395
Please, I love you!

30
00:03:38,395 --> 00:03:39,395
My Prince!

31
00:03:39,395 --> 00:03:41,395
I have ever since I was little.

32
00:03:41,395 --> 00:03:43,395
I've always loved you!

33
00:03:49,395 --> 00:03:50,395
Rue.

34
00:03:50,395 --> 00:03:55,395
He took Rue.

35
00:03:55,395 --> 00:03:56,395
You monster!

36
00:03:56,395 --> 00:03:57,395
Relax.

37
00:03:57,395 --> 00:03:59,395
I haven't killed her yet.

38
00:03:59,395 --> 00:04:01,395
She's deep in my stomach.

39
00:04:01,395 --> 00:04:04,395
I should have done this in that fight long ago

40
00:04:04,395 --> 00:04:06,395
and saved us all the trouble.

41
00:04:06,395 --> 00:04:08,395
She's just a human girl.

42
00:04:08,395 --> 00:04:13,395
I kidnapped on a whim and raised, but she's been quite useful.

43
00:04:13,395 --> 00:04:17,395
If you kill me, you'll be killing the girl within me as well.

44
00:04:17,395 --> 00:04:25,395
Likewise, if you steal me away, you have no choice but to offer up your heart to me.

45
00:04:25,395 --> 00:04:29,395
I can't fight even if I return the last heart shard. How horrible!

46
00:04:29,395 --> 00:04:33,395
Prince, I demand you give me your heart at once.

47
00:04:33,395 --> 00:04:34,395
It's hilarious.

48
00:04:34,395 --> 00:04:35,395
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

49
00:04:35,395 --> 00:04:37,335
Ha ha ha ha.

50
00:04:57,215 --> 00:04:58,955
Still resisting?

51
00:04:58,955 --> 00:05:03,835
You mean to imply you still have some chance of success, Prince?

52
00:05:06,395 --> 00:05:07,595
Princess Tutu.

53
00:05:07,895 --> 00:05:08,255
Yes?

54
00:05:08,955 --> 00:05:11,675
I would like for you to return my final heart shard.

55
00:05:12,055 --> 00:05:12,415
What?

56
00:05:13,515 --> 00:05:14,755
Please give it to me.

57
00:05:15,235 --> 00:05:16,295
I have to save her.

58
00:05:17,215 --> 00:05:18,015
No, I...

59
00:05:18,015 --> 00:05:20,015
I want to...

60
00:05:20,015 --> 00:05:20,915
save Rue.

61
00:05:23,555 --> 00:05:26,635
Excruciating pain of having Raven's blood eat at your heart.

62
00:05:27,235 --> 00:05:28,335
I know that pain.

63
00:05:29,275 --> 00:05:32,515
It starts in the weak places in your heart and spreads ruthlessly.

64
00:05:32,515 --> 00:05:36,835
You can't even stop yourself from hurting the people who are important to you.

65
00:05:39,295 --> 00:05:43,935
Rue has stood up under the burden of that suffering all alone ever since she was small.

66
00:05:44,995 --> 00:05:48,675
Her love was frail, and she was always afraid of losing love.

67
00:05:49,755 --> 00:05:51,935
The more she loved, the more she suffered.

68
00:05:52,475 --> 00:05:54,995
But there was no one she could even seek help from.

69
00:05:55,575 --> 00:05:57,695
But she never thought to stop loving.

70
00:05:57,695 --> 00:06:02,555
With words of true love, she led me out of the Raven's darkness.

71
00:06:04,255 --> 00:06:06,395
It's my turn to protect her now.

72
00:06:06,855 --> 00:06:09,815
And if possible, I'd like to take Rue as my princess.

73
00:06:11,135 --> 00:06:15,135
So, Princess Tutu, please give me the last heart shard.

74
00:06:16,275 --> 00:06:16,775
Yes.

75
00:06:16,775 --> 00:06:27,435
If your heart is not complete, I cannot gain eternal life from it.

76
00:06:27,775 --> 00:06:30,195
I almost rushed things in my eagerness.

77
00:06:32,055 --> 00:06:32,735
What?

78
00:06:34,915 --> 00:06:35,995
What's the matter?

79
00:06:36,655 --> 00:06:38,195
The pendant won't come off.

80
00:06:38,575 --> 00:06:39,855
What's going on?

81
00:06:40,315 --> 00:06:41,195
Why won't it?

82
00:06:41,195 --> 00:07:00,935
Princess Tutu, I grant you until dawn.

83
00:07:01,415 --> 00:07:05,035
You must give the final shard back to the prince by then.

84
00:07:05,035 --> 00:07:14,835
If you fail to do this, I will tear the prince's heart into pieces.

85
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:19,935
This tea is the blend that Drosselmeyer liked to drink while he was working.

86
00:07:20,675 --> 00:07:24,035
He used three parts Darjeeling and then added a psalm...

87
00:07:26,775 --> 00:07:30,095
Tell me again why I must do this?

88
00:07:31,015 --> 00:07:32,775
It certainly is noisy.

89
00:07:32,775 --> 00:07:40,775
What's going on?

90
00:07:41,295 --> 00:07:41,795
What?

91
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:46,975
Bathed in this noble blood, all people will become crows.

92
00:07:47,315 --> 00:07:50,375
Now celebrate my triumphant return.

93
00:07:51,115 --> 00:07:52,855
P.K. and Lillie?

94
00:07:54,315 --> 00:07:55,615
Mr. Cat?

95
00:07:55,995 --> 00:07:57,575
You'd better hurry.

96
00:07:57,915 --> 00:08:00,275
You haven't much time to do.

97
00:08:00,275 --> 00:08:21,235
I can't take it off.

98
00:08:21,315 --> 00:08:22,055
Why not?

99
00:08:22,475 --> 00:08:23,555
I wonder.

100
00:08:23,555 --> 00:08:26,555
This is bad for...

101
00:08:26,555 --> 00:08:30,555
Altor, I'm begging you, would you please be a little quiet...

102
00:08:30,555 --> 00:08:32,255
Well, well.

103
00:08:32,675 --> 00:08:36,295
That person writing at that desk looks a lot like me when I was younger.

104
00:08:36,555 --> 00:08:37,315
Could it be?

105
00:08:37,775 --> 00:08:39,075
No, I'm mistaken.

106
00:08:39,235 --> 00:08:41,095
I would never waver about writing.

107
00:08:41,555 --> 00:08:42,555
Ha ha ha ha ha ha.

108
00:08:43,555 --> 00:08:45,495
So you're Drosselmeyer.

109
00:08:45,495 --> 00:08:50,495
Hmm, these things all look a lot like what I use, but most of them appear to be fakes.

110
00:08:52,495 --> 00:08:55,495
You're trying to be responsible about your writing, aren't you?

111
00:08:56,495 --> 00:08:58,495
Well, that's why you can't write.

112
00:08:58,495 --> 00:09:03,495
You have to understand that when you're writing stories, you should do it more freely and irresponsibly.

113
00:09:04,495 --> 00:09:05,495
Just follow your own feelings.

114
00:09:05,495 --> 00:09:11,495
I have no desire to become like you, a demented, sadistic fossil who toys with people's fates for a lark.

115
00:09:12,495 --> 00:09:14,495
That thinking won't get us anywhere.

116
00:09:15,495 --> 00:09:16,495
Mewtwo!

117
00:09:17,495 --> 00:09:23,495
The Raven has revived and all of the Prince's heart has returned to him except for the shard in Princess Tutu's pendant.

118
00:09:24,495 --> 00:09:25,495
What?

119
00:09:25,495 --> 00:09:26,495
My hand's writing by itself.

120
00:09:26,495 --> 00:09:38,495
You see, you have my blood running through your veins.

121
00:09:39,495 --> 00:09:41,495
That was the lake called Despair.

122
00:09:42,495 --> 00:09:44,495
It was dark and deep just like Duck's eyes.

123
00:09:45,495 --> 00:09:47,495
What are you intending to make me write?

124
00:09:48,495 --> 00:09:50,495
The sorrowful yet beautiful story of Little Duck.

125
00:09:51,495 --> 00:09:52,495
The story of Duck?

126
00:09:52,495 --> 00:09:55,495
At that moment, Duck could hear a voice.

127
00:09:55,495 --> 00:09:59,495
It was the voice of Drosselmeyer, the man who controlled the story.

128
00:10:00,495 --> 00:10:01,495
Duck!

129
00:10:01,495 --> 00:10:06,495
It's because you're scared to let go of being Princess Tutu that you can't give back the heart shard, right?

130
00:10:07,495 --> 00:10:08,495
No, that's not it.

131
00:10:08,495 --> 00:10:11,495
You're afraid to part with the Prince.

132
00:10:11,495 --> 00:10:12,495
I just want...

133
00:10:12,495 --> 00:10:17,495
Rue would be carved into the Prince's heart for eternity because she gave herself over to the Raven.

134
00:10:17,495 --> 00:10:27,495
And by keeping the heart shard, Duck would live on in the Prince's heart as Princess Tutu and not as an ugly little Duck.

135
00:10:28,495 --> 00:10:30,495
Is it... is it all my fault?

136
00:10:31,495 --> 00:10:32,495
Yes, it is.

137
00:10:32,495 --> 00:10:36,495
And in order to take off the pendant, you'll have to lay down your life.

138
00:10:37,495 --> 00:10:42,495
Duck began to sink into the lake of despair, walking further and further in...

139
00:10:42,495 --> 00:10:43,495
Stop it!

140
00:10:44,495 --> 00:10:45,495
Don't go, Duck!

141
00:10:45,495 --> 00:10:47,495
Deeper and deeper...

142
00:10:47,495 --> 00:10:48,495
Stop it!

143
00:10:51,495 --> 00:10:52,495
What?

144
00:10:56,495 --> 00:10:57,495
Duck!

145
00:10:58,495 --> 00:10:59,495
Kier!

146
00:10:59,495 --> 00:11:01,495
There are crows all over town!

147
00:11:04,495 --> 00:11:05,495
Duck?

148
00:11:05,495 --> 00:11:06,495
Duck?

149
00:11:06,495 --> 00:11:07,495
Where did you go, Sora?

150
00:11:07,495 --> 00:11:08,495
Duck!

151
00:11:08,495 --> 00:11:09,495
Duck?

152
00:11:09,495 --> 00:11:10,495
Tuck?

153
00:11:11,495 --> 00:11:12,495
State...

154
00:11:16,495 --> 00:11:17,495
?!

155
00:11:17,495 --> 00:11:18,495
Quidditch!

156
00:11:19,495 --> 00:11:21,495
I've got to find...

157
00:11:22,495 --> 00:11:23,495
Don't go out there, it's dangerous!

158
00:11:23,495 --> 00:11:24,495
What?

159
00:11:24,495 --> 00:11:24,915
Never mind that!

160
00:11:24,995 --> 00:11:25,495
What happened to your hand?

161
00:11:26,495 --> 00:11:28,495
And when did you write a story?

162
00:11:28,495 --> 00:11:29,495
What happened?

163
00:11:29,495 --> 00:11:30,135
Tell me!

164
00:11:30,495 --> 00:11:34,495
Drosselmeyer came, and he Drosselmeyer?

165
00:11:34,495 --> 00:11:36,495
Drosselmeyer came, and he Drosselmeyer?

166
00:11:36,495 --> 00:11:38,495
Bastard made me write the story.

167
00:11:38,495 --> 00:11:41,495
You mean, Drosselmeyer was here in this room?

168
00:11:41,495 --> 00:11:42,495
Yes.

169
00:11:42,495 --> 00:11:43,495
Magnificent!

170
00:11:45,495 --> 00:11:46,495
What's wrong?

171
00:11:48,495 --> 00:11:49,495
Nothing.

172
00:11:49,495 --> 00:11:51,495
Hey, where are you going?

173
00:11:51,495 --> 00:11:52,495
Hey, wait!

174
00:11:54,495 --> 00:11:55,495
What's going on?

175
00:11:55,495 --> 00:11:58,495
It looks exactly like the Crow Festival scene

176
00:11:58,495 --> 00:12:00,495
that took place in The Prince and the Raven.

177
00:12:00,495 --> 00:12:04,495
So the Raven has cursed them.

178
00:12:04,495 --> 00:12:05,495
Damn it!

179
00:12:05,495 --> 00:12:06,495
Hey!

180
00:12:06,495 --> 00:12:08,495
The Raven's curse, is it?

181
00:12:08,495 --> 00:12:10,495
I wonder if she's alright then?

182
00:12:10,495 --> 00:12:13,495
The Lake of Despair, where is that?

183
00:12:15,495 --> 00:12:16,495
There you are, Zura!

184
00:12:16,495 --> 00:12:17,495
Uzura!

185
00:12:17,495 --> 00:12:19,495
That just disappeared, Zura!

186
00:12:19,495 --> 00:12:21,495
So you were with her when it happened?

187
00:12:21,495 --> 00:12:22,495
Where is she?

188
00:12:22,495 --> 00:12:23,495
This way, Zura!

189
00:12:28,495 --> 00:12:29,495
I'm sorry.

190
00:12:30,495 --> 00:12:32,495
I'm sorry, Rue.

191
00:12:33,495 --> 00:12:35,495
I'm sorry, Muto.

192
00:12:36,495 --> 00:12:38,495
If I vanish,

193
00:12:40,495 --> 00:12:42,495
the Heart Shard

194
00:12:42,495 --> 00:12:44,495
will return to you.

195
00:12:46,495 --> 00:12:47,495
This way, Zura!

196
00:12:49,495 --> 00:12:50,495
What?

197
00:12:50,495 --> 00:12:51,495
Outside the gate?

198
00:12:52,495 --> 00:12:54,495
I've never even thought of leaving this city.

199
00:12:54,495 --> 00:12:55,495
Now I see.

200
00:12:55,495 --> 00:12:57,495
I was being controlled by Drosselmeyer's story.

201
00:12:57,495 --> 00:12:58,495
That's why.

202
00:12:59,495 --> 00:13:02,495
It looks like the story started to spread beyond the city walls.

203
00:13:03,495 --> 00:13:04,495
What are you waiting for, Zura?

204
00:13:04,495 --> 00:13:05,495
Oh, sorry!

205
00:13:05,495 --> 00:13:06,495
Hurry up, Zura!

206
00:13:07,495 --> 00:13:08,495
Here, Zura!

207
00:13:08,495 --> 00:13:09,495
Here, Zura!

208
00:13:09,495 --> 00:13:10,495
Oh, sorry!

209
00:13:10,495 --> 00:13:11,495
Hurry up, Zura!

210
00:13:18,495 --> 00:13:19,495
Here, Zura!

211
00:13:20,495 --> 00:13:21,495
Doc!

212
00:13:25,495 --> 00:13:26,495
What's with this lake?

213
00:13:27,495 --> 00:13:29,495
For some reason, I can breathe.

214
00:13:30,495 --> 00:13:33,495
Is this just another stage setting Drosselmeyer prepared?

215
00:13:33,495 --> 00:13:41,495
I thought I was doing my best for Muto's sake.

216
00:13:42,495 --> 00:13:44,495
But was it for my own sake?

217
00:13:46,495 --> 00:13:48,495
Just like Mr. Drosselmeyer said,

218
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:53,495
I'm really thinking that I don't want to return Muto to the story.

219
00:13:53,495 --> 00:13:54,495
I'm really sorry.

220
00:13:56,495 --> 00:13:57,495
Doc!

221
00:13:59,495 --> 00:14:00,495
Doc!

222
00:14:01,495 --> 00:14:02,495
Doc!

223
00:14:03,495 --> 00:14:04,495
Vakir?

224
00:14:06,495 --> 00:14:07,495
Vakir!

225
00:14:11,495 --> 00:14:12,495
Doc!

226
00:14:13,495 --> 00:14:14,495
Vakir, the pendant won't come off.

227
00:14:15,495 --> 00:14:18,495
It's the last of Muto's heart shards.

228
00:14:19,495 --> 00:14:22,495
And Muto asked me to give it back to him, but...

229
00:14:23,495 --> 00:14:25,495
Muto said he wants to make Rue his princess.

230
00:14:26,495 --> 00:14:29,495
And I know he wants to save her from the raven.

231
00:14:31,495 --> 00:14:32,495
But it just won't come off.

232
00:14:33,495 --> 00:14:34,495
All this is my fault.

233
00:14:35,495 --> 00:14:37,495
Because I'm thinking that deep inside my heart,

234
00:14:38,495 --> 00:14:39,495
I don't want the story to ever end.

235
00:14:40,495 --> 00:14:44,495
Vakir and Lillie and Mr. Cat and the others turned into crows.

236
00:14:45,495 --> 00:14:46,495
But even after that...

237
00:14:48,495 --> 00:14:49,495
Idiot.

238
00:14:49,495 --> 00:14:50,495
You're not the only one.

239
00:14:50,495 --> 00:14:51,495
What?

240
00:14:51,495 --> 00:14:52,495
You're not the only one, Doc.

241
00:14:53,495 --> 00:14:54,495
I don't want to...

242
00:14:54,495 --> 00:14:58,495
No, the fact of the matter is that nobody wants to see the story come to an end.

243
00:14:59,495 --> 00:15:00,495
Nobody save Muto himself.

244
00:15:01,495 --> 00:15:04,495
I still can't write a story about Muto either.

245
00:15:04,495 --> 00:15:13,495
Stop blaming just yourself.

246
00:15:14,495 --> 00:15:17,495
Everyone is scared of being restored to their true selves.

247
00:15:18,495 --> 00:15:22,495
They're used to being given rules and stories that shelter them from the business of living.

248
00:15:22,495 --> 00:15:23,495
The real you is a duck.

249
00:15:23,495 --> 00:15:24,495
And the real me...

250
00:15:24,495 --> 00:15:36,495
In the end, the real me has been protected since my childhood.

251
00:15:36,495 --> 00:15:39,495
I can't protect anyone.

252
00:15:40,495 --> 00:15:45,495
But even if that is what I am truly like, I want to end the story once and for all.

253
00:15:46,495 --> 00:15:51,495
I want to protect Muto and you because of my own feelings, not some role given to me.

254
00:15:52,495 --> 00:15:53,495
Even if I use up all of my power.

255
00:15:53,495 --> 00:15:57,495
When that happens, I'll go back to being just a bird.

256
00:15:58,495 --> 00:16:00,495
And I won't ever study ballet with everybody again.

257
00:16:01,495 --> 00:16:02,495
That's fine, isn't it?

258
00:16:02,495 --> 00:16:04,495
After all, that's who you really are.

259
00:16:05,495 --> 00:16:06,495
Yeah.

260
00:16:06,495 --> 00:16:09,495
And even after that time comes, I will stay by your side forever.

261
00:16:10,495 --> 00:16:11,495
Fuck you.

262
00:16:11,495 --> 00:16:18,495
It's strange. Until a short while ago, I thought it was okay for me to simply vanish.

263
00:16:19,495 --> 00:16:21,495
But now, I'm weak.

264
00:16:22,495 --> 00:16:25,495
But for some reason, Fakir always makes me stronger.

265
00:16:26,495 --> 00:16:27,495
Somehow.

266
00:16:30,495 --> 00:16:32,495
Let's go back to being our true selves now.

267
00:16:33,495 --> 00:16:34,495
Yes.

268
00:16:34,495 --> 00:16:36,495
Let's compose an end for this story.

